## CSS Architecture

### Design Tokens

All values derived from a systematic scale. No magic numbers. `css/tokens.css` is the only owner
of the values; this file names tokens and roles, never their values.

The files are listed in the File Map above.

**Modular approach**: Each component type has its own CSS file for maintainability. Both pages link every file with its own `<link>`, in cascade order (tokens, reset, base, animations, components, utilities, main). No `@import`: it chains a request after main.css and delays first paint (audit PERF-2). A new CSS file gets a `<link>` in index.html and sobre.html, and an entry in `PRECACHE` in `sw.js` (the selftest fails without it).

### Color System (OKLCH)

OKLCH provides perceptually uniform colors - equal lightness values look equally bright to humans.

`css/tokens.css` owns the values; this lists the roles, one name each (audit 4.16). A component
uses the role, never a raw colour:

| Role | Token |
|---|---|
| Text, strong text (headings, links), secondary text | `--color-text`, `--color-text-strong`, `--color-text-secondary` |
| Values in form fields, text on the accent, errors | `--color-text-field`, `--color-text-on-accent`, `--color-error` |
| Page, surface, raised surface, card, opaque overlay (the copy menu) | `--color-bg`, `--color-surface`, `--color-surface-raised`, `--color-surface-card`, `--color-surface-overlay` |
| Accent (buttons, focus), its hover and 8% tint | `--color-accent`, `--color-accent-hover`, `--color-accent-soft` |
| Focus ring | `--color-focus-ring`, `--focus-ring-width`, `--focus-ring-offset` |
| Ink (black on light, white on dark), what borders and track tints are drawn with | `--color-ink` |
| Positive: the money-saved green of the savings bar | `--color-positive`, `--color-savings-bar-bg` |
| Borders | `--color-border`, `--color-border-strong`, `--color-border-dashed`, `--color-border-drag`, `--color-border-accent` |
| Glass (white edges and translucent fills) | `--color-highlight*`, `--color-divider*`, `--color-control*`, `--color-surface-sunken`, `--color-hover-tint`, `--color-press-tint` |

A tint of a role is derived from it, never typed as a colour: `oklch(from var(--color-accent) l c h
/ 0.08)`. Retheming the role then carries its tints, borders and rings along, and the dark block
restates a tint only when its opacity differs on dark (audit D-2). Shadows are black and the glass
is white in both themes, so those are plain `oklch(0% 0 0 / N)` and `oklch(100% 0 0 / N)`.

**Dark mode** follows the system (`prefers-color-scheme`, no toggle): the same roles get dark values
in one block at the end of `css/tokens.css`, and `color-scheme: light dark` turns the native controls
dark. The dark theme mirrors the light one: near-neutral surfaces (chroma 0.004) that rise 3 to 4
points of L per layer from the page at L 19% (`#131413`, the dark theme-color both pages declare),
with the green kept to text, links and the accent (audit D-1); the manifest keeps its one light
`theme_color`. A new colour is a role in both blocks, measured in both themes
(the Phase 4 lab runs axe and the contrast check with `dark`).

**Why OKLCH over HSL:**
- `oklch(50% ...)` green and `oklch(50% ...)` red look equally bright
- HSL lies - `hsl(120, 100%, 50%)` looks brighter than `hsl(240, 100%, 50%)`
- Better for generating accessible color scales

### Typography Scale

`css/tokens.css` owns the values. Each step has `--text-STEP-size`, `-leading` and `-tracking`
(xs, sm, base, md, lg, xl). Fluid only where it shows (audit L-3, question 3): the two heading
steps, lg (h2, 20 to 24 px) and xl (h1 and the typed amount, 24 to 30 px), grow with `clamp()` from
320 to 1280 px wide; UI text is static rem (12, 13, 15 and 17 px). Body text uses the
`--text-default-*` aliases. Leading is unitless, so it scales with the text (base: 1.4). Headings step down from h1
(xl) to h2 (lg), h3 (md) and h4 (body). Prices and quantities use `font-variant-numeric:
tabular-nums`; units ("/mês", "kWh/mês") are set in Inter like the text around them. `--font-mono`
is for code only. A `calc()` that needs the line box height multiplies: `var(--text-default-leading)
* var(--text-base-size)`.

### Spacing Scale

`--space-1` to `--space-8` (with `--space-1-5`, 6 px), static rem, so they respect the user's
font size and stay whole pixels. The vertical rhythm above the card, `--space-top-card`, is the
fluid one: 64 px at 320 to 128 px at 1280. `css/tokens.css` owns the values.

### Motion Tokens

craft:motion owns the values; `css/tokens.css` is the only place they are written:

| Token | For |
|---|---|
| `--duration-micro` / `-fast` / `-medium` / `-slow` | hover; dropdown and chevron; view swaps; the result card |
| `--duration-exit-fast` / `-exit-medium` | the closing side, about 80% of its enter |
| `--ease-emphasized-decelerate` | everything entering |
| `--ease-emphasized-accelerate` | exits only |

Rules: animate `transform` and `opacity` only (the tab indicator moves by transform; its width
snaps); no overshoot; a state that can flip mid-way uses a transition, not keyframes. Reduced
motion has one rule, in `css/reset.css`: every animation and transition becomes instant (`0s`).

### Layout

There are no layout utility classes: each component lays itself out in its own `css/components-*.css`,
with spacing from `css/tokens.css`. `css/utilities.css` holds only `.sr-only` and `.skip-link`.

