## Component Patterns

### Button States

Every button is one `.btn` in `css/components-buttons.css`, with its look on `data-variant`, its
height on `data-size` and, as in Foundations' Button, square as its own axis:

- `primary`: the accent fill (Comparar, both forms); `outline`: the glass edge (Sobre, Voltar, the
  result card's phone and website); `ghost`: no edge (tabs, the copy button, the copy chevron, menu
  items, the pill's ×).
- `data-square` (a boolean attribute): icon only, as wide as the size is tall, no padding (the copy
  chevron, the pill's ×, the result card's website). It combines with any variant and size.
- `sm` is 32 px (`--control-height-sm`), for controls inside a tray, menu or pill; `md` is 36 px
  (`--control-height-md`), for standalone actions. Every label is the UI text size.
- On touch screens (`pointer: coarse`) every control is at least 44 px: buttons, the logo and the
  fields grow to it, the household label covers its row, and the pill's × keeps its 32 px and takes
  taps over 44 px with an invisible `::after`. The desktop density is unchanged (audit C-4).
- States are written once, for every variant: hover inside `(hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)`,
  press `scale(0.97)` on `--duration-fast` (none with reduced motion), and `:disabled` or
  `aria-disabled="true"` (a busy submit stays focusable) without hover or press, in the secondary text
  colour. The focus ring is global, `:focus-visible` in `css/reset.css`.
- `aria-current="page"` (sobre.html's Sobre link) rests on the hover tint, without the outline's edge,
  shadow or press, so the current page reads as a place, not an action.
- A menu item that goes somewhere is an `<a class="btn">` (the ChatGPT and Claude items, with
  `target="_blank" rel="noopener"`); one that runs code is a `<button>`.

A component sets only its layout around the button (the tab indicator, the split button's group and
divider, the menu's position); it never restates the look. Text buttons are `.link-button`.

### Input States

Text fields and selects never render below 16 px (`max(1rem, ...)`): iOS Safari zooms into smaller fields on focus. `base.css` sets the floor for every control, and a component rule that sets its own size keeps it.

Numeric fields are `type="text" inputmode="decimal" enterkeyhint="go"`, with no `pattern`, `min` or
`max`, in a `novalidate` form: the browser's validation answers in its own language, and
`type="number"` reads "250,5" by the browser locale. `parseNumber` (`js/utils.js`) reads the value
("87,50", "87.50", "€ 80", "1.250"); `fieldError` (`js/main.js`) writes the PT-PT line and marks the
field with `aria-invalid` and `aria-describedby`. Keystrokes are never filtered, which would break paste
and autofill.

The field styles live in `css/components-input-views.css`.

### Result Animation

The keyframes live in `css/animations.css` and use the motion tokens above; neither file copies
the other's values.

